---
# Run locally with:
#   ANSIBLE_VAULT_PASSWORD_FILE=~/.nc-vault-pass ansible-lint .
# (reuses the same vault password file set up for scheduled backups - see
# docs/backup.md#scheduling). Without a vault password available, the five
# playbooks that load group_vars/vault.yml (backup.yml, restore.yml,
# playbook.yml, nextcloud-upgrade.yml, pg-major-upgrade.yml) fail their
# syntax-check step with a decrypt error instead of actually being linted.
#
# No CI wired up for this deliberately - see AGENTS.md.
#
# profile is deliberately `min`, not a stricter tier. The repo is clean at
# min, but `basic` and above flag ~6 command-instead-of-module findings for
# the streamed tar/rsync tasks (deliberate - the modules can't stream/behave
# the way those tasks need; each has a comment explaining why). Bumping the
# profile would just mean scattering `# noqa: command-instead-of-module`
# across intentional design decisions. Don't raise it without accounting for
# that.
profile: min
